  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution towards &#x201C;State of the World&apos;s Minorities&#x201D; annual report</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x201C;State of the World&apos;s Minorities&#x201D; is a yearly, in-depth global survey of major developments facing minority and indigenous communities around the globe. It is the only publication of its kind, and each year it focuses on a particular area of concern and how it impacts on minority communities, which so often lack the political power to have any input into decision making.   Recent years have focused on Land and Resource Rights (2012), Women&apos;s Rights (2011), Religious Minorities (2010) and Education (2009).  Aimed at governments, the EU and UN, humanitarian and advocacy organisations, and global public opinion generally, this publication aims to highlight the problems faced by indigenous minorities, thereby pushing governments to review policies and priorities, and supporting the ongoing campaign work of civil society organisations. All thematic editions include regional sections which highlight progress or problems for minorities in hot spots, high risk areas for minorities together with ground-breaking analysis commissioned from leading experts in the field and first- hand testimonies of representatives of minority communities, which attempt to pull together the extent and manifestations of the situation faced by minority communities when it comes to a specific issue.  Each report is launched with maximum publicity and media coverage, is immediately disseminated in print form to relevant decision makers, and is also readily available via the internet.</narrative>
  </description>
